Subject: [PATCH] logging(v2): retain unsigned metadata in native header
 rejection events

Convert four native header version/size/height diagnostics with the same
Info severity and readable messages. Keep unsigned claimed header values
separate from signed expected chain height. Rejection branches and checks
are unchanged; no header format, PoW, issuance or consensus changes.

Place only after bb045ac60ca (consensus(v2): connect native state, monetary
and script rules), and the shared generic registry prerequisite. These
native header producers and tests must not enter the eCash tier.

Add one focused native test covering all four public validation rejection
paths, UINT32_MAX version and UINT64_MAX claimed size/height, exact old
messages and numeric JSON. Header height uses bounded real regtest PoW;
size/version use existing public options that disable independent PoW and
Merkle checks. No private test hook or relaxed production validation.

Source-only: production event lint and diff checks pass; native tests have
not been compiled or run. Sealed381/current integration is unchanged.

